{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Create a new library with the given name. With git on PATH the library is born tracked: its data/<lib> is created inside a fresh git repo at repositories/<lib> (the same layout dev.github.import produces) and symlinked into the instance, the repo is registered in the dev.git registry (role library, autocommit on), and the autocommit sweeper makes its first commit within minutes - so canon never sees it and its history starts at creation. Without git it degrades to the plain data/<lib> directory, which the /data/* ignore rule still keeps out of canon.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::system_call::system_call;\nuse std::os::unix::fs::symlink;\n","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"}],"returntype":"String","type":"rust"},"id":"kqzknr19ec8a3ea32offa","readers":[],"time":1787329447085,"username":"system","writers":[]}